From b91cd8c27c5d07b630a8245652843757f7968724 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fermata Dev <dev@localhost>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 15:51:44 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Remove non-core addons and network VFS providers; keep core
 lean and stable
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Summary
-------
Strips the app down to its core media-player surface — YouTube, Web browser,
audio/video playback, local/SAF/M3U file explorer, and the MediaPlayer/
ExoPlayer/VLC engines — by removing optional addons and network file-system
providers. Changes are intentionally minimal and build-config driven where
possible (module exclusion), with small, safe source edits only where dead
wiring would otherwise remain.

Removed features
----------------
Addons (dynamic-feature modules):
  - TV / IPTV            (:tv)
  - Felex language tutor (:felex)
  - Google Cast          (:cast)
  - ChatGPT              (:chat)
  - POI (Android Auto)   (:poi)
Subtitle generator (disabled + impl modules removed):
  - :whisper, :mlkit, :opusmt   (on-device STT / translation impl modules)
  - 'subgen' addon left registered but hard-disabled (see below)
Network VFS providers (modules + core wiring):
  - SMB   (:smb)
  - SFTP  (:sftp)
  - Google Drive (:gdrive)

Retained core
-------------
  - Addons: YouTube + Web browser (both live in the retained :web module)
  - Engines: MediaPlayer (built-in), ExoPlayer (:exoplayer), VLC (:vlc)
  - File explorer backends: Local storage, SAF content:// trees, M3U playlists

Changes by file
---------------
settings.gradle
  - Replaced the single ':gdrive' + enableGoogleServices skip with an
    `excludedModules` set: tv, felex, cast, chat, poi, whisper, mlkit, opusmt,
    smb, sftp, gdrive. Excluded modules are no longer Gradle projects, so their
    `ext.addons` never aggregate into BuildConfig.ADDONS and they are dropped
    from dynamicFeatures. No core .java change needed for addon removal.

build.gradle (root)
  - 'subgen' addon entry: set `enabled: false`, `hasSettings: false`, and
    trimmed `depends` from 'exoplayer,translate' to 'exoplayer'.
    Rationale: SubGenAddon/TranslateAddon are compiled into :fermata core and
    referenced by the media engine, so they must remain in the registry to
    avoid a FermataAddon.findAddonInfo() RuntimeException at class-load. Leaving
    them registered-but-disabled keeps them inert: SubGenAddon.ENABLED defaults
    false, so MediaEngineManager/MediaEngineBase never force ExoPlayer for
    sub-gen, and the settings row is hidden (hasSettings=false). Dropping
    'translate' from depends prevents install attempts for the removed
    translate impl modules.

fermata/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml
  - Removed the Google Cast OptionsProvider <meta-data>
    (com.google.android.gms.cast.framework.OPTIONS_PROVIDER_CLASS_NAME →
    me.aap.fermata.addon.cast.CastOptionsProvider), which referenced a class
    that no longer ships after the :cast module removal.
  - Removed the unused android.permission.READ_PHONE_STATE permission
    (no code references anywhere in the project).

fermata/src/main/java/me/aap/fermata/vfs/FermataVfsManager.java
  - Removed all SMB/SFTP/Google Drive wiring: the GDRIVE/SFTP/SMB id and class
    constants, the ENABLE_* prefs, the constructor initProvider() calls, and the
    corresponding getProvider() switch cases.
  - Since gdrive was the last dynamically-installed network VFS, the now-dead
    dynamic-install machinery was removed too: addFileSystem(), loadProvider(),
    initProvider(), the private getProvider(...) overload, addProvider(),
    installModule(), and getActivity(), plus the now-unused imports
    (Context, StringRes, R, MainActivity, Promise, BooleanSupplier, Log,
    DynamicModuleInstaller, Pref, ActivityBase, VfsException, ENABLE_GS, failed).
  - Result: registers only the static filesystems (Local, Generic, Content/SAF,
    M3U); getProvider() serves only the 'm3u' scheme.

fermata/src/main/java/me/aap/fermata/ui/fragment/FoldersFragment.java
  - Removed the "Add folder" menu items for SFTP, SMB, and Google Drive and
    their handler branches in addFolder().
  - Removed the now-unused imports: BuildConfig.ENABLE_GS,
    FermataVfsManager.GDRIVE_ID / SFTP_ID / SMB_ID.
  - The "Add folder" menu now offers: File system, Content (SAF), M3U playlist.

Resulting addon registry (BuildConfig.ADDONS)
---------------------------------------------
  translate     (inert facade; no impl modules shipped)
  subgen        (hasSettings=false, enabled=false — disabled & hidden)
  youtube       (core, kept)
  web_browser   (core, kept)

Stability / safety notes
-------------------------
  - No core compile-time references to any removed addon/provider class remain
    (verified by codebase search).
  - SpeechRecognitionService stays declared but is unreachable in normal use
    (voice control uses the system RecognizerIntent, not this service); if it
    were ever invoked for sub-gen it fails gracefully via its onFailure handler
    (listener.error(ERROR_AUDIO)) rather than crashing.
  - Orphaned resource ids/strings (vfs_smb, vfs_sftp, vfs_gdrive, cast_addon,
    etc.) are intentionally left in place: unused resources are harmless and are
    stripped by R8 in release. Not removed to avoid churn across 18 locale files.
  - ENABLE_GS BuildConfig field and the google-services Gradle plugin are left
    as-is (general Google-Services switch, already false with no
    google-services.json present; out of scope for feature removal).
  - WRITE_EPG_DATA permission was deliberately NOT removed: it is used by the
    retained AtvInterface (Android-TV home-screen publishing of favorites/
    playlists), which is core and unrelated to the removed IPTV addon.

Verification
------------
  - ./gradlew projects → only :exoplayer, :fermata, :utils, :vlc, :web
  - ./gradlew :fermata:assembleMobileDebug → BUILD SUCCESSFUL
  - ./gradlew assembleMobileDebug (all retained modules) → BUILD SUCCESSFUL
  - Generated BuildConfig.ADDONS verified = {translate, subgen(disabled),
    youtube, web_browser}
